doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24404763
abstract: >
  Pycrograph is a GPLv3 Python desktop application for building
  publication figures from fluorescence microscopy images. Raw files
  (TIFF, including ImageJ and MetaMorph TIFF/STK) are registered by
  reference and never modified;
  every display setting (per-channel window, gamma, colour lookup table,
  orientation) is re-applied at render time. Provenance follows
  PysternBlot: SHA-256 source verification, hash-chained operation log
  and integrity reports.
keywords:
